<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81177" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιβώμ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>round the altar</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλεγος</span>
			 : Subst., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ π.</span>
			<i>images placed about the altar</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>2 Ch.</u>
				34.3
			</span></i>:—but <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιβωμόῳ</span></b>  (sic), <i>space round a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βωμός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rev.Hist.Rel.</u>
				97.275
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιβώμιοι, οἱ</span>, functionaries attached to Asiatic cults, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(3).1126
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Melos</span>) : hence
			<u>Peribomius</u>, name of an Archigallus, <i><span class="en">
				Juv.
				2.16
			</span></i>, cf.Sch.ad loc.</div>
